    {
      "slide_index": 2,
      "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c1_convolutional_graph_networks_two_wea",
      "chunk_index": 1,
      "chunk_id": "s02_c01",
      "text": "Convolutional graph networks have two weaknesses. Because their filters come from graph polynomials, they lack expressiveness on a small parameter budget.",
      "box": [
        0.05,
        0.2083,
        0.4391,
        0.2083
      ],
      "target_source": "svg"
    },
    {
      "slide_index": 2,
      "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c2_they_cannot_learn_hierarchical_multi",
      "chunk_index": 2,
      "chunk_id": "s02_c02",
      "text": "And they cannot learn hierarchical, multi-scale features alone, needing bolt-on tricks like clustering or node dropping.",
      "box": [
        0.5109,
        0.2083,
        0.4391,
        0.2083
      ],
      "target_source": "svg"
    },
    {
      "slide_index": 2,
      "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c3_image_cnns_neither_problem_local",
      "chunk_index": 3,
      "chunk_id": "s02_c03",
      "text": "Image CNNs have neither problem: local learning and shared filters naturally capture multi-scale patterns.",
      "box": [
        0.05,
        0.4417,
        0.4391,
        0.1778
      ],
      "target_source": "svg"
    },
    {
      "slide_index": 2,
      "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c4_but_their_euclidean_convolution_assu",
      "chunk_index": 4,
      "chunk_id": "s02_c04",
      "text": "But their Euclidean convolution assumes a regular grid, and does not fit irregular graphs.",
      "box": [
        0.5109,
        0.4417,
        0.4391,
        0.1778
      ],
      "target_source": "svg"
    },
    {
      "slide_index": 3,
      "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c1_why_not_borrow_euclidean_convolution",
      "chunk_index": 1,
      "chunk_id": "s03_c01",
      "text": "So why not borrow Euclidean convolution for graphs?",
      "box": [
        0.05,
        0.2083,
        0.9,
        0.1119
      ],
      "target_source": "svg"
    },
    {
      "slide_index": 3,
      "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c2_convolution_sensitive_spatial_order",
      "chunk_index": 2,
      "chunk_id": "s03_c02",
      "text": "Convolution is sensitive to spatial order, but graph networks must be permutation invariant.",
      "box": [
        0.05,
        0.3444,
        0.4391,
        0.2083
      ],
      "target_source": "svg"
    },
    {
      "slide_index": 3,
      "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c3_earlier_methods_picked_node_ordering",
      "chunk_index": 3,
      "chunk_id": "s03_c03",
      "text": "Earlier methods picked a node ordering independently of the convolution, so it could not be tuned for the task and often lost information.",
