      "slide_index": 5,
      "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c1_how_cocn_works_first_permutation",
      "chunk_index": 1,
      "chunk_id": "s05_c01",
      "text": "Here is how CoCN works. First, permutation generation regresses an absolute position for each node with an MLP on Laplacian-smoothed features, so similar nodes land nearby.",
      "box": [
        0.05,
        0.5083,
        0.2156,
        0.4
      ],
      "target_source": "svg"
    },
    {
      "slide_index": 5,
      "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c2_these_form_relaxed_permutation_matri",
      "chunk_index": 2,
      "chunk_id": "s05_c02",
      "text": "These form a relaxed permutation matrix, controlled by a factor tau that provably converges to a true permutation.",
      "box": [
        0.2781,
        0.5083,
        0.2156,
        0.4
      ],
      "target_source": "svg"
    },
    {
      "slide_index": 5,
      "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c3_nodes_row_cocn_slides_kernel",
      "chunk_index": 3,
      "chunk_id": "s05_c03",
      "text": "With nodes in a row, CoCN slides a kernel along the diagonal of the permuted edge and node matrices, extracting node features and their structure together.",
      "box": [
        0.5062,
        0.5083,
        0.2156,
        0.4
      ],
      "target_source": "svg"
    },
    {
